      "skos:definition": "Terms the WHO publications use under more than one name, recorded where a publication itself STATES that the names are equivalent. A shared spelling or a latent-semantic cosine is not evidence of equivalence and is never recorded here: each alternative label carries the source sentence that asserts it. Owner, 2026-09-30 (bean ftu0): the WHO glossary is owned by the style guide, where the house voices live. The style guide is a subgraph of who-iris since the owner's ruling of the same day (bean qsx4), so the glossary, the voices and the library they cite are one instance and every citation is a same-instance one.",
